---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { owner } from '../data/owner.mjs';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About Us | CheckVitalsNow"
  description="Who we are, what we write about, and the standards behind every CheckVitalsNow women's health guide."
  h1="About CheckVitalsNow"
  updated={false}
  pageType="AboutPage"
>
  <p>
    Many women's health questions get asked quietly, late at night, in a search bar. Why do I leak when I sneeze? Is this
    perimenopause? Why am I always so tired? The answers online are often buried under ads, scare stories, or products
    that promise a quick fix.
  </p>
  <p>
    {site.name} is an independent website that answers those questions in plain language. Our guides explain what is
    happening in your body, what tends to help, and when it is time to see a doctor, with links to the medical sources
    behind every claim.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Bladder health:</strong> leaking when you sneeze, frequent urination, Kegel exercises, bladder irritants,
      and bladder changes after menopause.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hormones and menopause:</strong> perimenopause symptoms, signs of hormonal imbalance, and bone health after
      menopause.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Energy and stress:</strong> the common causes of constant tiredness and practical ways to handle stress.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can find every guide in our <a href="/womens-health/">women's health section</a>.</p>

  <h2>Who is behind the site</h2>
  {
    owner.name ? (
      <p>
        {site.name} is owned and operated by {owner.name}. Guides are researched, written, and edited by the {site.name}{' '}
        editorial team.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>Guides are researched, written, and edited by the {site.name} editorial team.</p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    We are not doctors, and nothing on this site is medical advice. That is why we build every guide on primary sources,
    such as the National Institutes of Health, the CDC, MedlinePlus, and major academic medical centers, and link them at
    the end of each page. Please read our <a href="/medical-disclaimer/">medical disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    Our guides do not sell or promote products, and we never promise cures or quick fixes. When the research on a topic is thin, we say so. Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>
    explains how we research, write, and update every guide.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Spotted a mistake, or have a question you would like us to cover? Visit our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
